---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/image-bench.css';
---
<Layout title="Image Bench — resize, refine, take it with you" description="Crop, resize, compress and extract colors locally. A small image workbench, with no uploads.">
<section class="bench wrap" id="image-bench">
  <header class="bench-heading"><div><a href="/tools/" class="bench-back">← BACK TO THE TOOLBOX</a><h1>Image <em>Bench.</em></h1><p>A better fit. A lighter file. A useful palette.</p></div><span class="bench-stamp">LOCAL TO YOUR BROWSER<br/>NO UPLOADS / NO ACCOUNT</span></header>
  <div class="bench-toolbar" role="group" aria-label="Processing mode"><button data-image-mode="single" aria-pressed="true">Single image</button><button data-image-mode="batch" aria-pressed="false">Small batch · up to 10</button><span id="image-mode-hint">Precise crop, real encoded comparison, and colors to keep.</span></div>
  <div class="bench-drop" id="image-drop"><input id="image-files" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" hidden/><button id="image-open" class="bench-primary">Choose an image ↗</button><span>or drop / paste here · static PNG, JPEG, WebP<br/><small>20 MiB and 24 million pixels per image · batch total 100 MiB</small></span></div>
  <p id="image-status" class="bench-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Your originals stay untouched. Nothing is uploaded or automatically saved.</p>
  <noscript>Enable JavaScript to process images on your device.</noscript>
  <div class="bench-layout">
    <div class="bench-main"><section id="image-single"><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>The working image</h2><span id="image-source-info">NO IMAGE YET</span></div><div class="bench-canvas"><canvas id="image-canvas" tabindex="0" aria-label="Crop editor. Drag the crop or its corners. Arrow keys move one pixel, Shift moves ten. Hold Space or right-drag to pan. Focus then scroll to zoom."></canvas></div><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="image-fit">Fit</button><button id="image-actual">100%</button><button id="image-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">＋</button><button id="image-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button><button id="image-undo">Undo</button><button id="image-redo">Redo</button></div>
    <div class="bench-crop"><label>Crop ratio <select id="image-ratio"><option value="free">Free</option><option value="original">Original</option><option value="1">1:1</option><option value="1.3333333333">4:3</option><option value="1.5">3:2</option><option value="1.7777777778">16:9</option><option value="0.5625">9:16</option></select></label>{['x','y','width','height'].map(key=><label>Crop {key}<input id={`image-crop-${key}`} type="number" min={key==='x'||key==='y'?0:1} step="1"/></label>)}</div><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="image-rotate-left">Rotate −90°</button><button id="image-rotate-right">Rotate +90°</button><button id="image-flip-x">Flip horizontal</button><button id="image-flip-y">Flip vertical</button><button id="image-reset-crop">Full image</button></div><p class="bench-help">Rotation and flips reset the crop. Undo restores both. Numeric crop values allow precise free cropping.</p>
    <section class="bench-result" id="image-result" hidden><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>The actual result</h2><span id="image-result-info"></span></div><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="image-before" aria-pressed="false">Before encoding</button><button id="image-after" aria-pressed="true">After encoding</button><button id="image-result-fit">Fit</button><button id="image-result-actual">100%</button><button id="image-download" class="bench-primary">Download image</button></div><div class="bench-comparison" id="image-comparison"><img id="image-comparison-img" alt="Encoded image preview"/></div><p class="bench-help" id="image-result-detail"></p></section>
    </section><section id="image-batch" hidden><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>A small, orderly queue</h2><span>SEQUENTIAL PROCESSING</span></div><p class="bench-help">Shared fit dimensions, format and compression only. Single-image crops, rotation and flips are never applied to this queue.</p><div id="image-queue" class="bench-queue"></div><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="image-run-batch" class="bench-primary">Process pending images</button><button id="image-zip">Download completed ZIP</button></div></section>
    <section class="bench-palette" id="image-palette-panel"><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>Find its colors</h2><span>FROM THE CURRENT ENCODED RESULT</span></div><div class="bench-toolbar"><label>Colors <select id="image-color-count">{[3,4,5,6,7,8].map(n=><option selected={n===5}>{n}</option>)}</select></label><button id="image-extract">Extract palette</button><button id="image-palette-json">Download palette JSON</button><button id="image-send-palette">Prepare for Color Workshop ↗</button><a id="image-palette-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" hidden>Open Color Workshop ↗</a></div><div id="image-swatches" class="bench-swatches"></div><p class="bench-help">Near-transparent pixels are ignored. Shares are approximate. The editor opens in a new tab so your image stays here.</p></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="bench-settings"><div class="bench-section-title"><h2>Output settings</h2><span>NON-DESTRUCTIVE</span></div><label>Fit width / px <input id="image-max-width" type="number" min="1" max="8192" value="1600"/></label><label>Fit height / px <input id="image-max-height" type="number" min="1" max="8192" value="1600"/></label><label class="bench-checkbox"><input id="image-upscale" type="checkbox"/> Allow enlargement</label><p class="bench-help">Aspect ratio stays intact. Maximum 8192 per side and 16 million output pixels.</p><label>Format <select id="image-format"><option value="image/png">PNG · lossless / alpha</option><option value="image/jpeg">JPEG · opaque</option><option value="image/webp">WebP · alpha</option></select></label><label id="image-background-label">JPEG background <input id="image-background" type="color" value="#ffffff"/></label><label>Compression <select id="image-compression"><option value="quality">Quality control</option><option value="target">Target file size</option></select></label><label id="image-quality-label">Quality <output id="image-quality-value">85%</output><input id="image-quality" type="range" min="10" max="95" value="85"/></label><label id="image-target-label" hidden>Target / KiB <input id="image-target" type="number" min="1" max="102400" value="250"/></label><p class="bench-help" id="image-compression-help">PNG preserves pixels. JPEG and WebP use the quality setting.</p><div class="bench-toolbar"><button id="image-render" class="bench-primary">Update result</button><button id="image-cancel">Cancel</button><button id="image-clear">Clear images</button></div><p class="bench-help">Targets are best-effort, at most eight attempts. Dimensions are never reduced to meet a target. Results can be larger than the original.</p></aside>
  </div>
  <details class="bench-notes"><summary>Privacy, formats & limits</summary><p>Files are held in this tab only. Closing or refreshing loses them. Cross-tool transfers happen only after you ask, use temporary local storage, expire after five minutes and are deleted when read. Expired transfers are cleaned on the next visit.</p><p>Exports are rendered through the browser’s sRGB canvas path. Original EXIF/GPS and color profiles are not copied. Native browser encoders may differ; unsupported formats are disabled and never disguised with a different extension. HEIC, SVG, GIF, APNG and animated WebP are not supported.</p><p>Processing uses a worker where available and falls back to local serial processing otherwise. Old results are invalidated when settings change. A cancelled batch keeps completed results; ZIP output is limited to 100 MiB.</p></details>
</section><script>import '../../scripts/image-bench';</script>
</Layout>
